+++ b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/README.md
@@ -1,8 +1,8 @@
-# Offline dual-Panda contracts and codecs (P0/P1)
+# Offline dual-Panda contracts and codecs (P0/P1/P2)
 
 Standalone Python standard-library contracts and C++17 CAN codecs against
 openpilot `35e78a9d`, panda `a5919516`, opendbc `b3bd79a6`. This package is not
-imported by the active pandad and contains no device backend or installer.
+imported by the active pandad. P2 adds explicit native backends, without a runtime factory or installer.
 
 `profiles/unbound.json` loads with every identity/role unset and every permission
 false. Registry fixtures must explicitly use synthetic identities and supported
@@ -39,7 +39,51 @@ missing fixtures fail, never skip. The probe includes the pinned Panda `board/`
 and opendbc repository headers and reports host ABI only. Tests never import
 Panda, discover devices, compile MCU firmware or start the original pandad.
 
-P2–P7 still own real USB/SPI backends, runtime integration, connection epochs,
+P3–P7 still own runtime integration, connection epochs,
 whole-group freshness/safety barriers, F4 firmware, system-level fault handling
 and deployment packaging. Existing pandad startup/flash behavior is unchanged
 because this isolated package is not connected to that entry point.
+
+## P2 transport contract
+
+`transport.h/.cc` wraps a caller-owned backend and clock with a per-session lock,
+finite deadline and permanent cooperative cancellation. Results preserve actual
+bytes, confirmed prefixes, unknown remaining progress and the adapter's original
+status. Short reads return immediately; only known-zero-byte read timeouts can
+retry. Writes never replay, including after short completion, timeout or cancel.
+Uncertain/error writes poison that session; another board is never selected as
+fallback. One backend/clock/parser belongs to one session and must outlive callers.
+
+`usb_backend` selects a normal-firmware Panda by exact bound serial and DOS/RED
+software type, rejects ambiguity, and checks active configuration descriptors for
+interface0/alt0 bulk endpoints 0x81/0x03. It excludes bootstub/DFU and never detaches
+a driver, resets, clears halt or changes USB configuration/alternate setting.
+Construction and default `open_bound` are inert. Explicit device permission AND
+`bulk_alt0_verified=true` are required before enumeration. This flag is a future
+caller's evidence requirement, not proof from descriptors: the pinned firmware
+implements SET_INTERFACE but lacks GET_INTERFACE. No P0 profile can currently
+activate this C++ library, and actual alternate state remains unverified.
+
+`libusb_api` is real libusb code behind an injectable API. Every backend owns its
+context/handle. Native opening/claiming is outside the transfer-time contract.
+Tests inject a fake API; the native link smoke test only constructs an unopened
+object and exercises rejected default opening.
+
+`spi_backend` preserves successful current wire requests (4096-byte envelope,
+9-byte header, 7-byte reply header, little-endian ID and CRC32; 4032-byte chunks,
+first read1013). It emits each chunk once and never resends an uncertain request,
+including reads that may already have consumed the MCU queue. NACK returns Busy.
+The old concrete SPI files and active pandad path remain byte-identical. The new
+SPI adapter intentionally replaces old infinite/retry behavior with bounded
+errors; it does not claim error-path equivalence. No USB fallback exists.
+`linux_spi_io` links the real spidev syscalls and nonblocking flock, but has an
+inert constructor. Explicit open configures mode/bits/speed; it is never called
+by acceptance. A synchronous kernel ioctl cannot be forcibly cancelled here.
+
+The frozen budget table is `TIMING-BUDGET.md`. `timing_budget.h` is pure candidate
+health/heartbeat/queue policy; actual scheduler and whole-group barrier wiring
+remain P3/P4. Passing fake-clock tests is not a real-time hardware guarantee.
+The engineering validator `tools/validate_panda_transport.py` cleanly composes
+P0/P1/P2 patches, reruns P0/P1, and builds/tests P2 on macOS and Linux under
+network/device-node isolation. Linux includes real libusb and spidev linkage;
+it is a standalone transport target, not a full active pandad daemon build.
diff --git a/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/TIMING-BUDGET.md b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/TIMING-BUDGET.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dd0d417
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/TIMING-BUDGET.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# P2 candidate timing and resource budgets
+
+All times below are host monotonic microseconds unless marked ms. Freeze v1,
+2026-10-18, against openpilot35e78a9d/pandaa5919516. Numbers are candidate host
+policy, not measured C3XL/F4 performance. No live scheduler is installed.
+
+| Path | Bound / threshold | Rationale and tested behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Request read/write | caller1..100ms | finite replacement for timeout0/infinite; illegal0/101 rejected before backend |
+| Backend slice | at most5ms | pinned `panda.cc` CAN-send uses5ms; leaves scheduling opportunities within100Hz loop |
+| Lock wait | min(request budget,10ms) | one pinned pandad100Hz period; bounded Busy instead of shared-board blocking |
+| Wait quantum | at most1ms | cancellation and immediate-zero-timeout retry pacing; no busy loop |
+| Cancellation | next boundary; cooperative≤5ms while in backend,≤1ms waiting | permanent local atomic cancellation; no handle close/reset to interrupt IO; fake-clock bound only |
+| In-flight / pending queue | 1 / 0 | no accumulated commands or automatic replay; contenders only wait within lock budget; no FIFO fairness claim |
+| Control / bulk allocation | 4096 /16384 bytes | explicit bounded caller input; SPI control maximum4032 |
+| SPI envelope / chunk / first RX | 4096 /4032 /1013 bytes | locked original `panda_comms.h` and `spi.cc`, not historical2048-byte format |
+| SPI poll | ≤32 polls, waits≤100us, shared≤5ms deadline | finite even when fake time stops; polling reply does not resend request |
+| Health polling / maximum age | 100000 /250000 | `pandad.cc`100Hz with health every10frames; candidate allows two periods plus50ms margin; missing/future/age≥250000 invalid |
+| Heartbeat due / overdue | 100000 /250000 | same original10Hz scheduling; candidate host overdue threshold; NOT the MCU SILENT timeout |
+
+Request/backend/lock/deadline/cancel tests cover threshold−1, threshold,
+threshold+1 and exhausted/sub-millisecond remainder. Core clock wrap or backwards
+motion fails closed; SPI elapsed subtraction tolerates uint64 wrap, and outer
+Transport still rejects a backwards observation. Frozen pure age policy tolerates
+one uint64 wrap with elapsed<2^63 and rejects future/ambiguous samples. These are
+explicit contracts, not an assumption that all clocks have identical wrap policy.
+
+Health and heartbeat tests exercise pure policy only. P3/P4 must actually apply
+the thresholds to collected samples, scheduling, Event validity and group TX
+barriers; they do not authorize heartbeats or safety-mode commands in P2. No
+buffer from one handle is used by its sibling, but a failed required handle must
+still invalidate the whole control group during later integration.
+
+Native libusb open/claim and Linux spidev ioctl may exceed caller expectations
+inside OS/driver code. The wrapper detects late completion and preserves counts;
+it cannot preempt a stuck syscall. Offline evidence proves bounded algorithmic
+attempts and cooperative cancellation with compliant fake IO. Hardware timing,
+shutdown under a stuck driver, power loss and MCU heartbeat/SILENT remain untested.
diff --git a/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/libusb_api.cc b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/libusb_api.cc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9db86bb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/libusb_api.cc
@@ -0,0 +1,128 @@
+#include "libusb_api.h"
+
+#include <array>
+#include <utility>
+
+#include <libusb.h>
+
+namespace openpilot::pandad::compatibility {
+namespace {
+static_assert(LIBUSB_ERROR_TIMEOUT == kUsbTimeout && LIBUSB_ERROR_PIPE == kUsbPipe);
+static_assert(LIBUSB_ERROR_NO_DEVICE == kUsbNoDevice && LIBUSB_ERROR_INTERRUPTED == kUsbInterrupted);
+
+class NativeLibusbApi final : public LibusbApi {
+public:
+  ~NativeLibusbApi() override { shutdown(); }
+  int initialize() override {
+    if (context_) return kUsbBusy;
+    return libusb_init(&context_);
+  }
+  int enumerate(std::vector<UsbDeviceInfo> &devices) override {
+    if (!context_) return kUsbInvalid;
+    devices.clear();
+    libusb_device **list = nullptr;
+    const auto count = libusb_get_device_list(context_, &list);
+    if (count < 0) return static_cast<int>(count);
+    int result = kUsbSuccess;
+    for (decltype(count + 0) i = 0; i < count; ++i) {
+      libusb_device_descriptor desc{};
+      const int read_result = libusb_get_device_descriptor(list[i], &desc);
+      if (read_result != 0) { result = read_result; break; }
+      // Retain only normal-firmware Panda candidates. Bootstub and DFU are not
+      // opened, and unconfigured devices are reported without usable endpoints.
+      if ((desc.idVendor != 0xbbaa && desc.idVendor != 0x3801) || desc.idProduct != 0xddcc) continue;
+      UsbDeviceInfo info;
+      info.id = reinterpret_cast<UsbDeviceId>(libusb_ref_device(list[i]));
+      retained_.push_back(reinterpret_cast<libusb_device *>(info.id));
+      info.vendor = desc.idVendor;
+      info.product = desc.idProduct;
+      info.bcd_device = desc.bcdDevice;
+      info.serial_index = desc.iSerialNumber;
+      libusb_config_descriptor *config = nullptr;
+      if (libusb_get_active_config_descriptor(list[i], &config) == 0) {
+        info.active_configuration_known = true;
+        for (int n = 0; n < config->bNumInterfaces; ++n) {
+          const auto &interface = config->interface[n];
+          for (int a = 0; a < interface.num_altsetting; ++a) {
+            const auto &alt = interface.altsetting[a];
+            UsbAlternate item{alt.bInterfaceNumber, alt.bAlternateSetting, {}};
+            for (int e = 0; e < alt.bNumEndpoints; ++e) {
+              const auto &endpoint = alt.endpoint[e];
+              item.endpoints.push_back({endpoint.bEndpointAddress, endpoint.bmAttributes, endpoint.wMaxPacketSize});
+            }
+            info.alternates.push_back(std::move(item));
+          }
+        }
+        libusb_free_config_descriptor(config);
+      }
+      devices.push_back(std::move(info));
+    }
+    libusb_free_device_list(list, 1);
+    return result;
+  }
+  int open(UsbDeviceId device, UsbHandle &handle) override {
+    handle = 0;
+    libusb_device_handle *opened = nullptr;
+    const int result = libusb_open(reinterpret_cast<libusb_device *>(device), &opened);
+    if (result == 0) handle = reinterpret_cast<UsbHandle>(opened);
+    return result;
+  }
+  int serial(UsbHandle handle, std::uint8_t index, std::string &value,
+             std::uint32_t timeout_ms) override {
+    value.clear();
+    if (index == 0) return kUsbInvalid;
+    // libusb_get_string_descriptor_ascii uses an internal 1000ms timeout.
+    // Read LANGID and UTF-16LE descriptors explicitly with the requested slice.
+    std::array<unsigned char, 255> buffer{};
+    auto *native = reinterpret_cast<libusb_device_handle *>(handle);
+    int count = libusb_control_transfer(native, 0x80, LIBUSB_REQUEST_GET_DESCRIPTOR,
+                                       LIBUSB_DT_STRING << 8, 0, buffer.data(), buffer.size(), timeout_ms);
+    if (count < 0) return count;
+    if (count < 4 || buffer[1] != LIBUSB_DT_STRING || buffer[0] < 4 || buffer[0] != count || (buffer[0] & 1)) return kUsbIo;
+    const auto language = static_cast<std::uint16_t>(buffer[2] | (buffer[3] << 8));
+    count = libusb_control_transfer(native, 0x80, LIBUSB_REQUEST_GET_DESCRIPTOR,
+                                   static_cast<std::uint16_t>((LIBUSB_DT_STRING << 8) | index),
+                                   language, buffer.data(), buffer.size(), timeout_ms);
+    if (count < 0) return count;
+    if (count < 2 || buffer[1] != LIBUSB_DT_STRING || buffer[0] < 2 || buffer[0] != count || (buffer[0] & 1)) return kUsbIo;
+    for (int n = 2; n < buffer[0]; n += 2) {
+      if (buffer[n + 1] != 0 || buffer[n] < 33 || buffer[n] > 126) return kUsbIo;
+      value.push_back(static_cast<char>(buffer[n]));
+    }
+    return value.empty() ? kUsbIo : kUsbSuccess;
+  }
+  int claim(UsbHandle handle, int interface_number) override {
+    return libusb_claim_interface(reinterpret_cast<libusb_device_handle *>(handle), interface_number);
+  }
+  int control(UsbHandle handle, std::uint8_t type, std::uint8_t request,
+              std::uint16_t value, std::uint16_t index, std::uint8_t *data,
+              std::uint16_t length, std::uint32_t timeout_ms) override {
+    return libusb_control_transfer(reinterpret_cast<libusb_device_handle *>(handle), type,
+                                    request, value, index, data, length, timeout_ms);
+  }
+  int bulk(UsbHandle handle, std::uint8_t endpoint, std::uint8_t *data,
+           int length, int &actual, std::uint32_t timeout_ms) override {
+    actual = 0;
+    return libusb_bulk_transfer(reinterpret_cast<libusb_device_handle *>(handle), endpoint,
+                                 data, length, &actual, timeout_ms);
+  }
+  void release(UsbHandle handle, int interface_number) override {
+    libusb_release_interface(reinterpret_cast<libusb_device_handle *>(handle), interface_number);
+  }
+  void close(UsbHandle handle) override {
+    libusb_close(reinterpret_cast<libusb_device_handle *>(handle));
+  }
+  void shutdown() override {
+    for (auto *device : retained_) libusb_unref_device(device);
+    retained_.clear();
+    if (context_) libusb_exit(std::exchange(context_, nullptr));
+  }
+private:
+  libusb_context *context_ = nullptr;
+  std::vector<libusb_device *> retained_;
+};
+}  // namespace
+std::unique_ptr<LibusbApi> make_native_libusb_api() {
+  return std::make_unique<NativeLibusbApi>();
+}
+}  // namespace openpilot::pandad::compatibility
diff --git a/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/libusb_api.h b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/libusb_api.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..375f8f5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/libusb_api.h
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+#pragma once
+
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <memory>
+#include <string>
+#include <vector>
+
+namespace openpilot::pandad::compatibility {
+
+// Thin injectable seam. All return codes follow libusb's documented values;
+// constructing the native implementation does not create a context or list USB.
+inline constexpr int kUsbSuccess = 0;
+inline constexpr int kUsbIo = -1;
+inline constexpr int kUsbInvalid = -2;
+inline constexpr int kUsbAccess = -3;
+inline constexpr int kUsbNoDevice = -4;
+inline constexpr int kUsbNotFound = -5;
+inline constexpr int kUsbBusy = -6;
+inline constexpr int kUsbTimeout = -7;
+inline constexpr int kUsbOverflow = -8;
+inline constexpr int kUsbPipe = -9;
+inline constexpr int kUsbInterrupted = -10;
+
+using UsbDeviceId = std::uintptr_t;
+using UsbHandle = std::uintptr_t;
+struct UsbEndpoint {
+  std::uint8_t address = 0;
+  std::uint8_t attributes = 0;
+  std::uint16_t max_packet_size = 0;
+};
+struct UsbAlternate {
+  std::uint8_t interface_number = 0;
+  std::uint8_t alternate_setting = 0;
+  std::vector<UsbEndpoint> endpoints;
+};
+struct UsbDeviceInfo {
+  UsbDeviceId id = 0;
+  std::uint16_t vendor = 0;
+  std::uint16_t product = 0;
+  std::uint16_t bcd_device = 0;
+  std::uint8_t serial_index = 0;
+  bool active_configuration_known = false;
+  std::vector<UsbAlternate> alternates;
+};
+
+// One API instance belongs to one backend. Device IDs live until shutdown().
+// No detach/reset/clear-halt/configuration/alternate-setting mutation is exposed.
+class LibusbApi {
+public:
+  virtual ~LibusbApi() = default;
+  virtual int initialize() = 0;
+  virtual int enumerate(std::vector<UsbDeviceInfo> &devices) = 0;
+  virtual int open(UsbDeviceId device, UsbHandle &handle) = 0;
+  virtual int serial(UsbHandle handle, std::uint8_t index, std::string &value,
+                     std::uint32_t timeout_ms) = 0;
+  virtual int claim(UsbHandle handle, int interface_number) = 0;
+  virtual int control(UsbHandle handle, std::uint8_t type, std::uint8_t request,
+                      std::uint16_t value, std::uint16_t index, std::uint8_t *data,
+                      std::uint16_t length, std::uint32_t timeout_ms) = 0;
+  virtual int bulk(UsbHandle handle, std::uint8_t endpoint, std::uint8_t *data,
+                   int length, int &actual, std::uint32_t timeout_ms) = 0;
+  virtual void release(UsbHandle handle, int interface_number) = 0;
+  virtual void close(UsbHandle handle) = 0;
+  virtual void shutdown() = 0;
+};
+
+std::unique_ptr<LibusbApi> make_native_libusb_api();
+
+}  // namespace openpilot::pandad::compatibility
diff --git a/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/linux_spi_io.cc b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/linux_spi_io.cc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8b6afd1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/linux_spi_io.cc
@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
+#include "linux_spi_io.h"
+
+#ifdef __linux__
+#include <cerrno>
+#include <fcntl.h>
+#include <linux/spi/spidev.h>
+#include <sys/file.h>
+#include <sys/ioctl.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+
+namespace openpilot::pandad::compatibility {
+namespace {
+Status error_status(int error) {
+  switch (error) {
+    case ENODEV: case ENXIO: case ESHUTDOWN: return Status::Disconnected;
+    case ETIMEDOUT: return Status::Timeout;
+    case EBUSY: case EAGAIN: return Status::Busy;
+    case ECANCELED: return Status::Cancelled;
+    default: return Status::IoError;
+  }
+}
+}  // namespace
+
+LinuxSpiIo::~LinuxSpiIo() { close_device(); }
+
+Status LinuxSpiIo::open_device(const std::string &path, std::uint32_t speed_hz) {
+  if (fd_ >= 0 || path.empty() || speed_hz == 0 || speed_hz > 50000000) return Status::Invalid;
+  fd_ = ::open(path.c_str(), O_RDWR | O_CLOEXEC);
+  if (fd_ < 0) return error_status(errno);
+  // Configuration is an explicit hardware action too. Respect an existing
+  // user's bus lease before issuing any configuration ioctl.
+  const auto lock_status = begin(kBackendSliceMs);
+  if (lock_status != Status::Ok) {
+    close_device();
+    return lock_status;
+  }
+  std::uint32_t mode = SPI_MODE_0;
+  std::uint8_t bits = 8;
+  if (::ioctl(fd_, SPI_IOC_WR_MODE32, &mode) < 0 ||
+      ::ioctl(fd_, SPI_IOC_WR_MAX_SPEED_HZ, &speed_hz) < 0 ||
+      ::ioctl(fd_, SPI_IOC_WR_BITS_PER_WORD, &bits) < 0) {
+    const auto result = error_status(errno);
+    close_device();
+    return result;
+  }
+  end();
+  return Status::Ok;
+}
+
+void LinuxSpiIo::close_device() noexcept {
+  if (fd_ >= 0) {
+    end();
+    ::close(fd_);
+    fd_ = -1;
+  }
+}
+
+Status LinuxSpiIo::begin(std::uint32_t timeout_ms) {
+  if (fd_ < 0) return Status::Disconnected;
+  if (leased_ || timeout_ms == 0 || timeout_ms > kBackendSliceMs) return Status::Invalid;
+  // One nonblocking attempt. No flock wait can hold up another board.
+  if (::flock(fd_, LOCK_EX | LOCK_NB) < 0) return error_status(errno);
+  leased_ = true;
+  return Status::Ok;
+}
+
+void LinuxSpiIo::end() noexcept {
+  if (leased_) {
+    (void)::flock(fd_, LOCK_UN);
+    leased_ = false;
+  }
+}
+
+Result LinuxSpiIo::exchange(const std::vector<std::uint8_t> &tx, std::uint32_t timeout_ms) {
+  if (fd_ < 0) return {Status::Disconnected, 0, {}, true, false};
+  if (!leased_ || tx.empty() || tx.size() > kSpiBufferBytes || timeout_ms == 0 || timeout_ms > kBackendSliceMs) {
+    return {Status::Invalid, 0, {}, true, false};
+  }
+  std::vector<std::uint8_t> rx(tx.size(), 0);
+  spi_ioc_transfer transfer{};
+  transfer.tx_buf = reinterpret_cast<std::uintptr_t>(tx.data());
+  transfer.rx_buf = reinterpret_cast<std::uintptr_t>(rx.data());
+  transfer.len = static_cast<std::uint32_t>(tx.size());
+  // Never retry EINTR or timeout: the device may have handled the request.
+  const int count = ::ioctl(fd_, SPI_IOC_MESSAGE(1), &transfer);
+  if (count < 0) return {error_status(errno), 0, {}, false, true};
+  if (static_cast<std::size_t>(count) > tx.size()) return {Status::IoError, 0, {}, false, true};
+  rx.resize(static_cast<std::size_t>(count));
+  return {rx.size() == tx.size() ? Status::Ok : Status::Short, rx.size(), std::move(rx), true, false};
+}
+
+}  // namespace openpilot::pandad::compatibility
+#else
+#error "linux_spi_io.cc must only be compiled for Linux; pure SPI tests use SpiIo fakes"
+#endif
